  ["How do you do Miami in three days?", "Day one is the bay and the Art Deco strip with a sunset boat. Day two is Wynwood, Little Haiti and Little Havana on foot. Day three is the Everglades or the Florida Keys, depending on what you want more."],
  ["What is the best first thing to do in Miami?", "Get on the water. Almost everyone arrives on the beach and leaves having only seen the beach, and the skyline from Biscayne Bay is the thing people remember."],
  ["Should I do the Everglades or the Keys in three days?", "Everglades if you want wildlife and landscape, and it is half a day each way. Keys if you want a boat trip and a drive, and it is a longer, more spread-out day. Do not try both."],
